<title>CHINA: Southern China subway gets $18.1 million loan.</title>
<headline>Southern China subway gets $18.1 million loan.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The China Construction Bank has granted a 150 million yuan ($18.1 million) loan to the first subway line in the south China city of Guangzhou, the People's Daily said on Thursday.</p>
<p>By the end of June this year, the Guangzhou Metro Project had received 6.75 billion yuan in financing for its 18.4 km first phase.</p>
<p>The first phase, begun in 1993 and scheduled to be completed in 1997, is expected to cost a total of 15.6 billion yuan.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
</text>
